[[127,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/939011215\">Op. 7025B18 BOOT LID LINING - R+R</a></p><p>1. Undo the badge retaining nuts.</p><p>2. Working from outside the boot compartment, remove the badge.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/939001962.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[127,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Check that the badge is not damaged.</p><p>- Position the badge.</p><p>- Tighten the nuts.</p><p><a href=\"#/939011215\">Op. 7025B18 BOOT LID LINING - R+R</a></p>"]]